docs {
  # jWallet Lite mock API

  Start the backend first: `cd backend && npm start`. State resets on every
  restart, so run the collection against a fresh server for the balances
  in the tests to match.

  The `local` environment holds the base URL and the only token the mock
  accepts (`mock_access_token_123`).

  Folders run in order. `4 Transfer` is a story: send a transfer, retry it
  with the same Idempotency-Key (same transactionId, no second deduction),
  reuse the key with a different payload (409), then the failure cases.
}
